.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH orgsidian-parse 1  "parse " 
.SH NAME
orgsidian\-parse \- Parse an org file and print its AST
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorgsidian parse\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Parse an org file and print its semantic AST.
.PP
By default the AST is rendered as a human\-readable headline tree (best\-effort presentation — the exact format is not a stability contract). With \-\-json the full semantic document is printed as pretty JSON with camelCase keys; the JSON shape mirrors the current semantic types and is NOT yet a schema\-stability contract (the stable wire surface arrives with the GUI IPC layer).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the AST as pretty JSON (camelCase keys) instead of the human\-readable tree
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
Path to the `.org` file to parse
